  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Research on Improving Systems of Education (RISE) Programme Evaluation</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Evaluation of the Research on Improving Systems of Education Programme will run from June 2024 to March 2025, and aims to document lessons learned and impact case studies, to inform future education research initiatives. By enhancing accountability for a substantial Foreign Commonwealth and Development Office investment, the Evaluation will identify outcomes and impacts of RISE activities in Ethiopia, Tanzania, and Pakistan. It seeks to extract transferable lessons for global education research programmes, particularly regarding cost, complexity, and gender integration. The primary audience is Foreign Commonwealth and Development Office (including its Education, Gender, and Inclusion Research Team), the Girls&#x2019; Education Department, and relevant country offices.</narrative>
  </description>
